{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["And the reason for <b>\"that he may give it to me\" וְיִתְּנֶנָּה לִי</b> is that I will reckon it as a gift, even if I take it for full silver from him. Therefore he did not mention the language of sale. And likewise, <b>\"You shall sell me food for silver, and give me water for silver\"</b> (Deuteronomy 2:28) — the water given as a gift, I will give silver for it. Or it is simply the way of the language to express it thus in transactions of sale." "<b>The cave of Machpelah</b> — the language of Rashi: a house with an upper story above it. Another interpretation: that it was doubled in pairs (Eruvin 53a). And this is not correct, for Scripture says, <b>\"Ephron's field which was in the Machpelah\"</b> (Genesis 23:17), and behold it is the name of the place in which the field is located, and there is no need to seek a reason for the names of places. And in Bereshit Rabbah (58:8) they said that the Holy One, blessed be He, doubled the stature of the first man, and his grave is inside it. And according to their view, that entire place was called thus from eternity, and they did not know the reason for it, for Ephron, in the price of the field, sold him everything with the understanding that there was no grave there. And behold, Abraham sought only that he sell him the cave, for it is at the edge of the field, and the field would remain for Ephron. But he said to him, by way of courtesy or deception, that he would give him the field and the cave that is in it, for it is not fitting for a distinguished man such as him to have the cave as a burial possession while the field belongs to another. And Abraham rejoiced in this and acquired everything for the money that he mentioned to him."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {1 "Ramban cites Eruvin 53a by page number only; the folio reference is rendered as given."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:33:48.006279523Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}